<!DOCTYPE html>
<html class="brand-color-background antialiased" lang="en" data-theme="light" style="font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    <!-- Primary Meta Tags -->
    <title>Free Color Contrast Checker for WCAG AA and AAA - Coffee &amp; Fun LLC</title>
    <meta name="title" content="Free Color Contrast Checker for WCAG AA and AAA - Coffee &amp; Fun LLC" />
    <meta name="description" content="Check the contrast between any two colors, see whether it passes WCAG AA or AAA, and get a fixed color that does. Free, instant, and works right in your browser." />
    <meta name="author" content="Coffee &amp; Fun LLC" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />

    <!-- Canonical URL -->
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/contrast-checker/" />

    <!-- Favicon -->
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/images/brand/favicon.png" sizes="any" />

    <!-- Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Coffee &amp; Fun" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Free Color Contrast Checker for WCAG AA and AAA" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Check the contrast between any two colors, see whether it passes WCAG AA or AAA, and get a fixed color that does. Free, instant, and works right in your browser." />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/contrast-checker/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/assets/images/social/pages/contrast-checker.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Color Contrast Checker card showing a pass badge and a contrast ratio" />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />

    <!-- Twitter Card -->
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:site" content="@bycoffeeandfun" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Free Color Contrast Checker for WCAG AA and AAA" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Check the contrast between any two colors, see whether it passes WCAG AA or AAA, and get a fixed color that does." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/assets/images/social/pages/contrast-checker.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="Color Contrast Checker card showing a pass badge and a contrast ratio" />

    <meta name="theme-color" content="#fef5ec" />

    <!-- Structured Data -->
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@graph": [
          {
            "@type": "WebApplication",
            "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/contrast-checker/#app",
            "name": "Color Contrast Checker",
            "description": "Check the contrast ratio between a text color and a background color, see whether it meets WCAG 2.1 AA or AAA for normal and large text, and get the nearest color that passes.",
            "url": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/contrast-checker/",
            "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication",
            "operatingSystem": "Web Browser",
            "offers": {
              "@type": "Offer",
              "price": "0",
              "priceCurrency": "USD"
            },
            "featureList": [
              "WCAG 2.1 contrast ratio calculation",
              "AA and AAA results for normal and large text",
              "Live preview of real text at several sizes",
              "Suggests the nearest color that passes",
              "Shareable link that restores both colors",
              "Copies ready to paste CSS",
              "Runs entirely in the browser with no uploads"
            ],
            "publisher": { "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/#organization" },
            "creator": { "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/#founder" },
            "isAccessibleForFree": true,
            "inLanguage": "en"
          },
          {
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/contrast-checker/#faq",
            "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/#website" },
            "mainEntity": [
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "What is a good color contrast ratio?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "WCAG 2.1 asks for at least 4.5:1 between normal sized text and its background, and at least 3:1 for large text. Level AAA raises that to 7:1 for normal text and 4.5:1 for large text. Higher is easier to read, and 4.5:1 is the number most teams are held to."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "What counts as large text in WCAG?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "Large text means at least 24px, or at least 18.66px when the text is bold. Anything smaller counts as normal text and needs the higher 4.5:1 ratio. Font size is measured as rendered on screen, so a heading scaled down on mobile can drop out of the large text bracket."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Does contrast apply to buttons, icons and form fields?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "Yes. WCAG 1.4.11 Non-text Contrast asks for at least 3:1 between a user interface component and what sits next to it. That covers button edges, input borders, focus rings, toggle states and the meaningful parts of icons. A border you can barely see against the page fails this even when the text inside it passes."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Is contrast ratio the same as brightness?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "No. Contrast ratio compares relative luminance, which weights green most heavily, then red, then blue. That is why bright yellow on white fails badly while the same yellow on black passes easily, and why two colors that look equally bold can score very differently."
                }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Does passing a contrast check mean my site is accessible?",
                "acceptedAnswer": {
                  "@type": "Answer",
                  "text": "No. Contrast is one success criterion out of many. A page can pass every contrast check and still be unusable with a keyboard, unlabelled for a screen reader, or impossible to follow without color. Treat this as one check in a wider review."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
            "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/contrast-checker/#breadcrumbs",
            "itemListElement": [
              { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/" },
              { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Apps and tools", "item": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/apps/" },
              { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Color Contrast Checker" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    </script>

    <script src="https://unpkg.com/vue@3"></script>

    {% bundledCss %}
    {% pageCss "contrast-checker" %}
    {% include sketch-styles.liquid %}
{% include schema-org.liquid %}

    </head>

<body>
    <a href="#tool" class="skip">Skip to the checker</a>

    {% assign showMiddleBadgeWithText = true %}
    {% include header.liquid %}
{% raw %}
    <main v-cloak id="main-content" class="wrap">

        <header id="tool">
            <h1 class="brand-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl">Color contrast checker</h1>
            <p class="lede">Pick a text color and a background color. You get the contrast ratio, a plain answer about whether it passes, and if it does not, a color that does.</p>

            <div class="sketch-note sketch-float" style="top: -14px; right: -4%; --sketch-rotate: 9deg;">
                <svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path d="M12 2 L13.5 10.5 L22 12 L13.5 13.5 L12 22 L10.5 13.5 L2 12 L10.5 10.5 Z" class="sketch-sparkle"/>
                </svg>
            </div>
        </header>

        <!-- Announced to screen readers whenever the verdict changes. -->
        <div class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite">{{ announcement }}</div>

        <!-- ===== Step 1: the two colors ===== -->
        <section class="cf-step" aria-labelledby="h-colors">
            <h2 class="step-label" id="h-colors">1. Your two colors</h2>

            <div class="color-grid">
                <div class="color-field">
                    <label class="field-label" for="cc-text">Text color</label>
                    <div class="color-row">
                        <input type="color" id="cc-text-swatch" class="swatch" v-model="textInput"
                               aria-label="Text color, visual picker" />
                        <input type="text" id="cc-text" class="hexbox" v-model="textInput"
                               inputmode="text" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"
                               aria-describedby="cc-text-help" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="field-help" id="cc-text-help">Hex value, for example #3d2b1f</p>
                </div>

                <div class="swap-cell">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm cf-swap" @click="swap"
                            style="--btn-color: var(--color-mocha); --btn-fg: #fff"
                            aria-label="Swap the text and background colors">
                        <span aria-hidden="true">&#8646;</span> Swap
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="color-field">
                    <label class="field-label" for="cc-bg">Background color</label>
                    <div class="color-row">
                        <input type="color" id="cc-bg-swatch" class="swatch" v-model="bgInput"
                               aria-label="Background color, visual picker" />
                        <input type="text" id="cc-bg" class="hexbox" v-model="bgInput"
                               inputmode="text" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"
                               aria-describedby="cc-bg-help" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="field-help" id="cc-bg-help">Hex value, for example #fef5ec</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p v-if="parseError" class="field-error" role="alert">
                <span aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span> {{ parseError }}
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- ===== Step 2: the answer ===== -->
        <section class="cf-step" aria-labelledby="h-result">
            <h2 class="step-label" id="h-result">2. The answer</h2>

            <div class="verdict" :class="verdictClass">
                <p class="ratio"><span class="ratio-num">{{ ratioText }}</span><span class="ratio-unit">:1</span></p>
                <p class="verdict-line">
                    <span class="verdict-mark" aria-hidden="true">{{ passesAANormal ? '✓' : '✗' }}</span>
                    {{ verdictSentence }}
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- The preview is the point of the tool, so it shows real text, at real sizes. -->
            <div class="preview" :style="{ background: bgHex, color: textHex, borderColor: previewBorder }">
                <p class="pv-lg">Large heading text</p>
                <p class="pv-bold">Bold 18.66px text</p>
                <p class="pv-normal">Normal body text at 16px, the size most paragraphs actually use.</p>
                <p class="pv-small">Small print at 13px, the size that fails most often.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="preview-note">A preview of your two colors. Everything above sits on {{ bgHex }} with {{ textHex }} text.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- ===== Step 3: the WCAG detail ===== -->
        <section class="cf-step" aria-labelledby="h-levels">
            <h2 class="step-label" id="h-levels">3. What it passes</h2>

            <ul class="levels">
                <li v-for="lv in levels" :key="lv.key" class="level" :class="lv.pass ? 'is-pass' : 'is-fail'">
                    <span class="level-state">
                        <span class="level-mark" aria-hidden="true">{{ lv.pass ? '✓' : '✗' }}</span>
                        <span class="level-word">{{ lv.pass ? 'Pass' : 'Fail' }}</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="level-name">{{ lv.name }}</span>
                    <span class="level-need">needs {{ lv.need }}:1</span>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="levels-note">Large text means 24px or bigger, or 18.66px and bigger when bold.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- ===== Step 4: the fix ===== -->
        <section class="cf-step" v-if="suggestion" aria-labelledby="h-fix">
            <h2 class="step-label" id="h-fix">4. Make it pass</h2>
            <div class="fix">
                <p class="fix-copy">
                    The closest {{ suggestion.which }} color that reaches {{ suggestion.target }}:1 is
                    <code>{{ suggestion.hex }}</code>, giving {{ suggestion.ratio }}:1.
                </p>
                <div class="fix-actions">
                    <span class="fix-chip" :style="{ background: suggestion.previewBg, color: suggestion.previewFg }" aria-hidden="true">Aa</span>
                    <button type="button" class="btn cf-apply" @click="applySuggestion"
                            style="--btn-color: var(--color-cocoa); --btn-fg: #fff">
                        Use {{ suggestion.hex }}
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ===== Step 5: take it with you ===== -->
        <section class="cf-step" aria-labelledby="h-share">
            <h2 class="step-label" id="h-share">5. Take it with you</h2>
            <div class="share-actions">
                <button type="button" class="btn cf-share" @click="copyCss"
                        style="--btn-color: var(--color-cocoa); --btn-fg: #fff">
                    {{ copiedCss ? 'Copied ✓' : 'Copy the CSS' }}
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline cf-share" @click="copyLink"
                        style="--btn-color: var(--color-cocoa)">
                    {{ copiedLink ? 'Copied ✓' : 'Copy a link to this check' }}
                </button>
            </div>
            <pre class="css-out"><code>color: {{ textHex }};
background-color: {{ bgHex }};</code></pre>
        </section>

        <!-- ===== Reference content ===== -->
        <section class="cf-step explainer" aria-labelledby="h-about">
            <h2 class="step-label" id="h-about">How color contrast is measured</h2>
            <p>Contrast ratio compares the relative luminance of two colors on a scale from 1:1, two identical colors, to 21:1, pure black on pure white. Luminance is not the same as how bright a colour looks to the eye: green counts for far more than red, and red for far more than blue. That is why a vivid yellow can fail against white while sailing past on black.</p>
            <p>WCAG 2.1 sets the bar at <strong>4.5:1 for normal text</strong> and <strong>3:1 for large text</strong> at level AA, the level most legislation and procurement rules point at. Level AAA raises it to 7:1 and 4.5:1. Success criterion 1.4.11 adds a separate <strong>3:1 minimum for user interface components</strong>, which is the one people forget: input borders, focus rings, button edges and the meaningful parts of icons all have to clear it.</p>
            <p>Contrast is necessary but it is not sufficient. Passing every check here does not make a page accessible on its own. Text still needs to be resizable, controls still need names, and nothing should rely on color alone to carry meaning. If you want a deeper reading tool, we also build <a href="https://www.helperbird.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Helperbird</a>, and the rest of what we make is on our <a href="/apps/">apps and tools</a> page.</p>

            <h2 class="step-label" id="h-faq">Common questions</h2>
            <div class="faq">
                <details class="qa">
                    <summary>What is a good color contrast ratio?</summary>
                    <p>Aim for 4.5:1 or better on normal text. That is the WCAG AA threshold and the number most teams are measured against. Large text can drop to 3:1, and AAA asks for 7:1. Higher is genuinely easier to read, especially in bright light or on a cheap screen.</p>
                </details>
                <details class="qa">
                    <summary>What counts as large text?</summary>
                    <p>At least 24px, or at least 18.66px if the text is bold. It is measured as rendered, so a heading that shrinks on mobile can quietly fall out of the large text bracket and start needing 4.5:1 instead of 3:1.</p>
                </details>
                <details class="qa">
                    <summary>Do buttons and borders need to pass too?</summary>
                    <p>Yes, at 3:1, under WCAG 1.4.11. A pale hairline border around an input is the classic failure: the text inside passes comfortably while the control itself is nearly invisible against the page.</p>
                </details>
                <details class="qa">
                    <summary>Why do two colors that look similar score so differently?</summary>
                    <p>Because the formula weights green about seven times more than blue. Swapping a blue for a green of the same apparent brightness can move the ratio a long way, in either direction.</p>
                </details>
                <details class="qa">
                    <summary>Does my data leave the browser?</summary>
                    <p>No. The whole calculation runs in this page. There is no upload, no account and no analytics inside the tool.</p>
                </details>
            </div>
        </section>

        <p class="foot">Everything is worked out in your browser, nothing you pick is sent anywhere.</p>
    </main>
{% endraw %}

    {% include modals.liquid %}
    {% include footer.liquid %}

    {% pageJs "contrast-checker" %}
</body>
</html>
